  "description": "timing.v1 §2.2, §2.3, §2.5: a resolved resource, or a requirement, -> its declaration. resource.kind is the authoring kind (stream, state, event, operation; @stream is read as stream). Its annotations are either annotations, already resolved, or layers {defaults, kind_defaults, resource}, which a reader merges key by key, resource over kind_defaults over defaults (core §9.3). A requirement case gives requirement.annotations, a [requires.<role>]'s own. The vocabulary is timing.period_ms, timing.deadline_ms and timing.lifespan_ms; another key under timing. is no key of it. expect.declaration is one of: \"not_this_profiles\" (no key of the vocabulary); \"ignored\" (a key of the vocabulary, whatever its value, on a state, an event, an operation or a requirement: it means nothing there, and a linter warns of it); \"invalid\", with reasons, in this order, each key checked alone: period_value, deadline_value, lifespan_value (a key present whose value is not an integer from 1 to 2^53-1; an integral float is that integer, so 20.0 is 20, and -0.0 is 0, which is no value; a string, a boolean, an array or a table is no value); or \"declared\", for a stream, with period_ms, deadline_ms and lifespan_ms, each the integer, or null when absent, and below_period: true exactly when both a period and a deadline are declared and the deadline is below the period (no deadline, §2.5)."
